<h1>physics_fixture_create</h1>
<p>The first step in setting up a fixture is creating it with this function. The returning index should be stored in a variable to be used in all further functions that are used to define and use this fixture.</p>
<div data-conref="../../../../assets/snippets/Note_physics_fixture_define.hts">
<p class="note"><span data-conref="../../../../assets/snippets/Tag_note.hts"><span class="note">NOTE</span></span> You can only define a fixture within a room that has <a href="../../../../The_Asset_Editors/Room_Properties/Room_Properties.htm#physics">Physics</a> enabled.</p>
</div>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">physics_fixture_create()</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_ID_PhyFixture"><a target="_blank" href="physics_fixture_create.htm">Physics Fixture ID</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">fix_Ball = physics_fixture_create();</p>
<p>The code above will create a fixture and store its index in the variable &quot;fix_Ball&quot;.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
